  "id": "2026-09-12-large-documents-deep-contract",
  "scope": "large-documents",
  "kind": "review",
  "date": "2026-09-12",
  "question": "Which costs require fewer mounted nodes, and what selection, find and export guarantees survive partial DOM coverage?",
  "model": "GPT-6 / Codex",
  "method": "best-api/deep-design-v2; plite-research/source-probes; plite-plan; history-v2",
  "trigger": "User requested: go even deeper $task plan / research, this is a huge api. Planning/research only; the provisional design was reopened.",
  "requirements": [
    "Ordinary rendering must not omit document content because of size; explicit viewport permission applies to nested paginated units as well as top-level roots.",
    "Preserve the exact mounted host, active descendants, native input/composition, canonical selection/change/history/collaboration and root-local coverage.",
    "Compare delete/merge/reuse above the existing public nouns; account for current product, proof and teaching consumers with source-bound evidence.",
    "Separate pagination canvas geometry from generic measured block flow; no public coordinate protocol solely to compensate for duplicated ownership.",
    "Finish deep research and concrete prototype/adoption gates without claiming an unimplemented renderer or source-uncertain/native-device proof accepted."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Reconciled the original eight-group assessment, prior design, 111-row manifest and E19-E23/endpoint-retention research. Freshly traced native lifetime, pagination unit omission and clipboard policy composition; six pinned local reference repositories and CSSWG draft add specific proof requirements. Original inconclusive browser packet remains excluded. AST re-enumeration reconciles 126 bounded rows and an 83-path adoption census.",
  "summary": "Prefer one explicit omission permission and stable active DOM; delete pagination’s second generic viewport/coordinate owner and keep its existing canvas. Withdraw public fragment normalization and the new root marker. Source-stable probes expose host/child replacement, implicit paginated unit filtering, mixed copy-policy failure, static dependency reachability and SSR omission. Runtime adoption remains gated.",
  "verdict": "defer",
  "previous": "2026-09-11-large-documents-rendering-design",
  "relation": "supersedes",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep/configure: reject requiring every consumer to override auto; full remains the complete-DOM control, with its cold cost measured separately.",
    "Change API: prefer virtualize on existing Editable/PlateContent and a boolean pagination permission; no mode taxonomy, public threshold, page-layout arrays, generic offset or public diagnostic callback.",
    "Add primitive: no public virtualizer factory, async loader, global window/height store or capability certificate earns a job. Reuse committed root coverage and scheduler for materialization.",
    "Delete/merge: delete automatic segments/staged accumulation, range-keyed virtual groups, inert find metadata and duplicated pagination projection; preserve semantic hiding and actual native/clipboard responsibilities.",
    "Move ownership: pagination owns mounted roots, page/unit windows, navigation and one existing canvas coordinate frame; ordinary flow keeps a measured viewport backend. Projection-only comparison passes, real renderer proof is still required.",
    "Replace architecture: keep a dedicated virtual component/subpath as the material challenger if single-entrypoint dependency, cold rendering or stable-parent proof fails. DOM-present containment is a separate measured experiment; no copied height-tree rewrite."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "Five current-contract package probe cases and three projection cases pass. JSDOM proves host/key/clipboard behavior only; pagination used injected 400px rectangles and the fixture retained all DOM children. Page comparison proves root-key/canvas-extent parity and property-read counts at 100/1000/10000 supplied page items, not total layout cost, speed or native geometry. Actual runtime build kept 475 inputs stable; Node SSR covered nine cases, with no window/document. Proposed calls typecheck only as declarations. No production target, hydration, native Find UI, AT, print, real IME/device, collaboration or packed clean-install/application-bundle acceptance. Sequential same-thread comparison; no independent workers or model-family review. P0-P4 and S1-S7 are planned, not implemented.",
